(207714, 11918, 2690, '<td valign="top">I like this concept but it is way to dark. I would have shown more of the diamond as well, possibly more than one! (like there are more laying around). maybe a starburst filter and some hidden glass to reflect. still a good concept.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-02-10 12:42:30.</i></td>', 'I like this concept but it is way to dark. I would have shown more of the diamond as well, possibly more than one! (like there are more laying around). maybe a starburst filter and some hidden glass to reflect. still a good concept.', '2003-02-04 16:13:37.000000', '2003-02-10 12:42:30.000000', 1),
(207825, 11970, 1041, '<td valign="top">challenge met.  so, how did you do this ... 2 bottles, moved one?  that''s the only thing i can come up with that would match the photo.  great idea :)  i like that your photo is basically b&amp;w except for the whiskey which has a nice warm color to it.  good job filling the frame with the subject, too.</td>', 'challenge met.  so, how did you do this ... 2 bottles, moved one?  that''s the only thing i can come up with that would match the photo.  great idea :)  i like that your photo is basically b&w except for the whiskey which has a nice warm color to it.  good job filling the frame with the subject, too.', '2003-02-04 17:53:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(207826, 11920, 1041, '<td valign="top">challenge met.  i hope people look at your photo long enough to understand it, it took me a second.  i really like the idea, i almost submitted something similar to the "something new" challenge.  the difficult thing to control is that the flower in the background is so bold and dominant in its color that it overpowers the remains of the flower in the foreground (or is it a bud?)  it also draws the eye to the out of focus part of the photo.  anyway, love the colors, i would probably have zoomed out just a tad so you didn''t clip the edges of the blooming flower.  because it''s so little that''s chopped off it looks accidental rather than on purpose.  :)</td>', 'challenge met.  i hope people look at your photo long enough to understand it, it took me a second.  i really like the idea, i almost submitted something similar to the "something new" challenge.  the difficult thing to control is that the flower in the background is so bold and dominant in its color that it overpowers the remains of the flower in the foreground (or is it a bud?)  it also draws the eye to the out of focus part of the photo.  anyway, love the colors, i would probably have zoomed out just a tad so you didn''t clip the edges of the blooming flower.  because it''s so little that''s chopped off it looks accidental rather than on purpose.  :)', '2003-02-04 17:55:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(207828, 11816, 1041, '<td valign="top">challenge met.  i had something very similar in mind for this challenge, i''m glad i didn''t submit it, because yours is way better  :)  i like the setup, how the before and after are connected by the 2nd wineglass being partially behind the first and in front of the first candle.  the candles are a nice addition that suggest passage of time.  the one thing that i would''ve maybe tried differently is to use red wine.  it would go better with the candles.  good job.</td>', 'challenge met.  i had something very similar in mind for this challenge, i''m glad i didn''t submit it, because yours is way better  :)  i like the setup, how the before and after are connected by the 2nd wineglass being partially behind the first and in front of the first candle.  the candles are a nice addition that suggest passage of time.  the one thing that i would''ve maybe tried differently is to use red wine.  it would go better with the candles.  good job.', '2003-02-04 17:57:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(207829, 11779, 1041, '<td valign="top">LOL, this could be my hubby''s breakfast.  when we started dating i used to complain that he used a papertowel for a plate.  must be a bachelor thing.  ;)  i like the contrast between the bread and the toast, i think that would''ve been even further emphasized if you had skipped the butter.  also, a different color background to make the papertowel stand out a bit more would''ve been nice.  overall, still a good idea for this challenge :)</td>', 'LOL, this could be my hubby''s breakfast.  when we started dating i used to complain that he used a papertowel for a plate.  must be a bachelor thing.  ;)  i like the contrast between the bread and the toast, i think that would''ve been even further emphasized if you had skipped the butter.  also, a different color background to make the papertowel stand out a bit more would''ve been nice.  overall, still a good idea for this challenge :)', '2003-02-04 17:59:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(207876, 12033, 1280, '<td valign="top">Meets the challenge but is a little dark on my monitor....could just be mine.</td>', 'Meets the challenge but is a little dark on my monitor....could just be mine.', '2003-02-04 19:08:32.000000', NULL, 1),
