(211822, 11737, 4046, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your comments.<br/>For those who wanted to see how I did this photo, please have a look at:<br/><a href="//photo.marsebion.com/dpc/baa/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//photo.marsebion.com/dpc/baa/</a> <br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-02-11 10:22:37.</i></td>', 'Thank you all for your comments.For those who wanted to see how I did this photo, please have a look at://photo.marsebion.com/dpc/baa/ ', '2003-02-10 03:16:45.000000', '2003-02-11 10:22:37.000000', 0),
(211842, 12045, 1829, '<td valign="top">CC:  Great example of catching the motion of the egg white dropping into the bowl.  I love how you have used black as your primary background colour with the white bowl.  It really stands out.  The yellow from the egg of course adds a nice colourful touch. I also like how you have added the two eggs beside the bowl, using the whole frame instead of leaving it black in that area.  The composition of your photo is excellent, by the way you have placed the eggs, bowl and hand all in one.  The lighting is also crisp, light and clear and is easily seen.  Just a little flaw is the shadow which takes your eye straight to it, but with a little moving of light and perhaps even another light may take away the shadow, however it''s just a small thing.  I think the way the hand holds the egg looks like it''s been cracked like a true non professional chef, which is a good thing because it''s all natural and hey who can crack an egg like a pro (not me).  Anyway overall a top shot, keep up the fantastic work and I look forward to seeing more of your photo''s in the near future.  PS: Hope your not a chef (didn''t mean to offend if you are)</td>', 'CC:  Great example of catching the motion of the egg white dropping into the bowl.  I love how you have used black as your primary background colour with the white bowl.  It really stands out.  The yellow from the egg of course adds a nice colourful touch. I also like how you have added the two eggs beside the bowl, using the whole frame instead of leaving it black in that area.  The composition of your photo is excellent, by the way you have placed the eggs, bowl and hand all in one.  The lighting is also crisp, light and clear and is easily seen.  Just a little flaw is the shadow which takes your eye straight to it, but with a little moving of light and perhaps even another light may take away the shadow, however it''s just a small thing.  I think the way the hand holds the egg looks like it''s been cracked like a true non professional chef, which is a good thing because it''s all natural and hey who can crack an egg like a pro (not me).  Anyway overall a top shot, keep up the fantastic work and I look forward to seeing more of your photo''s in the near future.  PS: Hope your not a chef (didn''t mean to offend if you are)', '2003-02-10 04:44:50.000000', NULL, 0),
